6.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal\;font-family:Arial;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:justify">This entity has no form that can be understood by a material being, and can hardly be understood in spiritual or ideal contexts, for it represents every single form in e\very possible and impossible context. Its appearance is everchanging in a quantum style by the observer effect of all who witness it, with its best description being a fractalic distortion of any element related to its observer, therefore, having a differ\ent appearance to each observer.</span></p></body>)/Rect[422.076 270.39 577.685 336.242]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj137 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(   Universe.)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg /Helv 10 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 10.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240920235135-03'00')/NM(bb138ce29a0f43518600d4a0c15c9228)/Page 1/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="font-family:Helvetica">   Universe.</span></p></body>)/Rect[273.661 275.412 340.261 287.612]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj138 0 obj<</BS 172 0 R/Contents(The final entity of the campaign, and one of the possible culprits for the weirdness and chaos that permeate this universe. This entity has properties beyond the comprehensible, of divine level or even bigger. The most elemental of what it could be consid\ered çontologicalé. This entity has no specific name, for no name truly represents a concept that could be attributed to a çcallé for it, and at the same time, every single name represents it perfectly, therefore, any 5 random letters could be considered \a name for it. \(If you want to make things funnier, try rolling a d5 each turn for a new name!\), making it impossible to be documented in a definite manner. Found in the Nexus, the çheart of the Foundational Spaceé \(or it maybe could be said that it IS\ the Nexus?\), there is no definite manner to reach it by any H9P character until now, but on a meta level, the creator deemed that to reach it, your character needs to reach level -10, while on the Foundational Space. It cannot be de facto çdefeatedé, fo\r its existence is inherent to existence and nonexistence themselves, so çkilling ité, çdefeating ité or çceasing its existenceé have little to no effects, at maximum being temporary setbacks, although it can be done, even if its moot to try.  It is extre\mely powerful, being able to shape reality itself, but only showing hostility to those who are hostile to it. The objective this entity represents is a kind of çendpointé for the campaign, being recommended for it to be used mainly as a çfinal bossé, or a\s some manner to achieve your ultimate goal, because achieving it equals to finishing the story, so this creature should equal being its final step.)/CreationDate(D:-001-1-1-1-1-1-00'30')/DA(0 0 0 rg /Arial 9 Tf)/DS(font: Arial,sans-serif 9.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240920235758-03'00')/NM(d7acb930cdb148c288da8a71ac95f1c3)/Page 1/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:9.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal\;font-family:Arial;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:justify">The final entity of the campaign, and one of the possible culprits for the weirdness and chaos that permeate this universe. This entity has properties beyond the compreh\ensible, of divine level or even bigger.</span><span style="font-size:8.0pt;text-align:justify"> </span><span style="text-align:justify">The most elemental of what it could be considered &#8220;ontological&#8221;. This entity has no specific name, for no \name truly represents a concept that could be attributed to a &#8220;call&#8221; for it, and at the same time, every single name represents it perfectly, therefore, any 5 random letters could be considered a name for it. \(If you want to make things funni\er, try rolling a d5 each turn for a new name!\), making it impossible to be documented in a definite manner. Found in the Nexus, the &#8220;heart of the Foundational Space&#8221; \(or it maybe could be said that it IS the Nexus?\), there is no definite m\anner to reach it by any H9P character until now, but on a meta level, the creator deemed that to reach it, your character needs to reach level -10, while on the Foundational Space. It cannot be de facto &#8220;defeated&#8221;, for its existence is inhere\nt to existence and nonexistence themselves, so &#8220;killing it&#8221;, &#8220;defeating it&#8221; or &#8220;ceasing its existence&#8221; have little to no effects, at maximum being temporary setbacks, although it can be done, even if its moot to try. <\/span><span style="text-align:justify"> It is extremely powerful, being able to shape reality itself, but only showing hostility to those who are hostile to it. The objective this entity represents is a kind of &#8220;endpoint&#8221; for the campaign, bei\ng recommended for it to be used mainly as a &#8220;final boss&#8221;, or as some manner to achieve your ultimate goal, because achieving it equals to finishing the story, so this creature should equal being its final step.</span></p></body>)/Rect[45.3301 46.664 571.342 206.874]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj139 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents( Dif x10)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 21.8 Tf)/DS(font: Helvetica,sans-serif 21.8pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240917140210-03'00')